aintains two pungs and flexibility for the Dots tiles.\n\nReason: F2 is the least useful tile in my hand. It cannot form any melds with my current tiles, and with only one F2 remaining unshown, the chance of forming a pung is minimal. Discarding F2 preserves my two existing pungs (B8\u00d73 and F3\u00d73) and keeps my B2 and B4 pairs, which could potentially form sequences or pungs to complete my winning hand.\n\nAnswer: Play F2"}
